::  GENERATED by tools/gen-mc-tests.py -- do not edit.
::  Expected values are normalized tlc2.TLC output at the pinned commit.
/+  *test
/=  check  /lib/check
|%
++  trim
  ::  drop blank lines; TLC's blank separators between trace states carry
  ::  no information and the captured golden has them removed
  |=  w=wain
  ^-  wain
  (skip w |=(l=@t =('' l)))
::
++  verdict-only
  ::  R2.7.6.2: the projection for a case whose counter-example WITNESS is
  ::  nondeterministic at the pin (six runs of the same jar gave six different
  ::  loop states). Keeps the verdict, the counter-example header and the
  ::  counts; drops the numbered trace -- the discipline `gen-dfid-tests.py`
  ::  already applies to a DFID counterexample, for the same reason: where
  ::  tlc2's own answer varies run to run, no port can match it and no oracle
  ::  says what matching would mean
  |=  w=wain
  ^-  wain
  %+  skim  w
  |=  l=@t
  ?|  =('Error:' (end [3 6] l))
      =('Model checking' (end [3 14] l))
      =('The depth' (end [3 9] l))
      !=(~ (find "states generated" (trip l)))
  ==
::
++  test-mc-act-label-params
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  ^-  wain
    :~
        'Error: Deadlock reached.'
        'Error: The behavior up to this point is:'
        'State 1: <Initial predicate>'
        'x = <<0, 0>>'
        'State 2: <Inc(1) line 8, col 11 to line 8, col 53 of module spec>'
        'x = <<1, 0>>'
        'State 3: <Inc(1) line 8, col 11 to line 8, col 53 of module spec>'
        'x = <<2, 0>>'
        'State 4: <Op(1,"a") line 9, col 13 to line 9, col 78 of module spec>'
        'x = <<2, 1>>'
        'State 5: <Op(1,"a") line 9, col 13 to line 9, col 78 of module spec>'
        'x = <<2, 2>>'
        '5 states generated, 5 distinct states found, 0 states left on queue.'
        'The depth of the complete state graph search is 5.'
    ==
  !>
  %-  trim
  %+  check:check
    '---- MODULE spec ----\0a\\* R4.2n: a trace step through a parametrized action is labelled with the\0a\\* action operator\'s arguments, `<Inc(1) ...>` and `<Op(1,"a") ...>`\0a\\* (`Action.getLocation`); the port printed `<Inc ...>`.\0aEXTENDS Naturals\0aVARIABLE x\0aInit == x = [p \\in 1..2 |-> 0]\0aInc(p) == x[p] < 2 /\\ x\' = [x EXCEPT ![p] = x[p] + 1]\0aOp(n, s) == x[1] = 2 /\\ x[2] < 2 /\\ s = "a" /\\ x\' = [x EXCEPT ![2] = x[2] + n]\0aNext == (\\E p \\in {1} : Inc(p)) \\/ (\\E s \\in {"a"} : Op(1, s))\0a====\0a'
  'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0a'
